// fixture-442 (rfc-resolution-semantics.md §3 Axis W — W1): Axis D folded
// into a workspace, SUCCESS side — a `resolution { }` block declared on
// the WORKSPACE ROOT is legal and applies as the effective policy for the
// WHOLE workspace resolve, not just the root package itself.
//
// member-a and member-b each require a DIFFERENT named/index dep
// (widget-a / widget-b) that offers three versions (1.0.0/1.5.0/2.0.0).
// With no `resolution` block the default `maxver` strategy would pick
// 2.0.0 for both. Both resolve to 1.0.0 here — proving the root's
// `resolution { strategy "minver" }` is genuinely the effective policy
// for EVERY member's resolve, not merely parsed-and-ignored. See
// fixture-443 for the companion member-scope REJECTION (a member may not
// declare its own `resolution { }` block).
resolution {
    strategy "minver"
}
workspace {
    member "member-a"
    member "member-b"
}
